    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "All six monitored lemur species in Madagascar used bridges to cross roads and pipelines.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Nine studies across Australia, Brazil, and Peru documented that rope bridges were used by a range of mammal species.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Seven studies showed that between three and 25 mammal species utilized rope bridges.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "One study confirmed that arboreal marsupials using rope bridges did not experience high predation rates during crossing attempts.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "No evidence was found for the effects of green bridges, or overpasses, specifically on primate populations.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "A significant research gap exists regarding the effects of green bridges on primate populations.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Studies on general overpass structures for terrestrial mammals show promising results.",
