    "statement": "Twenty-two studies found that overpasses were used by a wide range of mammals including rodents, carnivores, ungulates, bears, and marsupials.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Four studies demonstrated that overpasses combined with fencing reduced vehicle-mammal collisions.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Tunnel and underpass installations showed effectiveness for various terrestrial mammal species.",
    "citations": []
  },
  {
    "statement": "Specific data for primate use of tunnels and underpasses is limited.",
    "citations": []
  }
]

[
  {
    "statement": "Several actions can be implemented at research and tourism sites to reduce disease transmission from humans to wild primates.",
